      "text.about": "# Welcome\n\nThis site carries the sacrament meeting program and the ward duty rosters.",
      "text.closing_thanks": "Thank you to the speakers, to the brethren for administering the sacrament, to the accompanist, the chorister, the ushers, the interpreter, and to all others who took part in this meeting. We welcome you back to our meetings next Sunday!",
      "text.internal": "# Bishopric tool",
      "text.ordination_footer": "Those in favor may show it by the uplifted hand. [Pause briefly.] Those opposed, if any, may also show it. [Pause briefly.]",
      "text.ordination_header": "We propose that the following (receive the Aaronic Priesthood and) be ordained:",
      "text.releases_footer": "Those who wish to express thanks for his/her/their service may do so by raising their hand. [Pause.]",
      "text.releases_header": "The following have been released with thanks from their callings in the ward:",
      "text.sacrament_intro": "We will prepare for the sacrament by singing the sacrament hymn. After the hymn, the sacrament will be blessed and passed to the congregation.",
      "text.sacrament_prayers": "Blessing on the bread\nO God, the Eternal Father, we ask thee in the name of thy Son, Jesus Christ, to bless and sanctify this bread to the souls of all those who partake of it, that they may eat in remembrance of the body of thy Son, and witness unto thee, O God, the Eternal Father, that they are willing to take upon them the name of thy Son, and always remember him and keep his commandments which he has given them; that they may always have his Spirit to be with them. Amen.\n\nBlessing on the water\nO God, the Eternal Father, we ask thee, in the name of thy Son, Jesus Christ, to bless and sanctify this water to the souls of all those who drink of it, that they may do it in remembrance of the blood of thy Son, which was shed for them; that they may witness unto thee, O God, the Eternal Father, that they do always remember him, that they may have his Spirit to be with them. Amen.\n\nThank you for your reverence during the sacrament. Next ...",
      "text.sustaining_footer": "Those in favor of sustaining him/her/them may do so by raising their hand. [Pause.] If any are opposed, they may also so indicate. [Pause.]",
      "text.sustaining_header": "The following have accepted a call to serve in the ward [Please stand]",
      "text.ward_business": "Official ward business",
      "text.welcome": "Welcome to the sacrament meeting of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints",
      "text.welcome_footer": "All who wish to welcome them to the ward may show it by raising their hand.",
      "text.welcome_header": "We warmly welcome to our ward the following who have recently been baptized/moved in",
